SHELL - Computah OS library
(generated from docs/API.md)

Running programs and command lines. Syntax: see
man sh or OS.md.

shell.execute(command) -> ok, code

Runs a command line (pipes, redirection, ;, &&,
||, &, variables, globs) and waits for it, except
for background jobs. Returns success and the exit
code or error.

shell.run(program, ...) -> ok, code

Runs one program by name with arguments and waits
for it.

shell.spawn(program, args[, streams[, detached]]) -> thread

Starts a program as a new process without waiting.
args is a list; streams may set stdin, stdout,
stderr. Returns the thread, or nil, reason.

shell.resolve(name[, extension]) -> path

Finds a program: with an extension ("lua"),
searches $PATH; names containing / are resolved
directly. Returns nil, reason if not found.

shell.load(path) -> function, env

Loads a program file with a fresh environment
based on the globals.

shell.parse(...) -> args, options

Splits arguments into plain arguments and options:
-abc sets a, b and c; --name=value sets name; --
ends options.

  local args, opts = shell.parse(...)
  if opts.v then print("verbose") end

shell.parseLine(command) -> entries

Parses a command line into {pipeline = {commands},
background, op} entries without running it.

shell.getWorkingDirectory() -> path

The current process's working directory.

shell.setWorkingDirectory(path) -> boolean

Changes the working directory. Returns nil, "not a
directory" if it isn't one.

shell.getAlias(name) -> string

What an alias stands for, or nil.

shell.setAlias(name, value)

Defines an alias (or removes it with nil): typing
name runs value, with further words passed on.
Defaults: ll, la, dir, cls, ?.

shell.aliases() -> iterator

Iterates over aliases: for name, value in
shell.aliases() do ... end.

shell.getPath() -> string

The program search path ($PATH).

shell.setPath(path)

Sets the program search path.

shell.builtins

Table of shell builtins (cd, pwd, set, unset,
alias, unalias, exit); add functions to make your
own.
